ts":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md","old_string":"2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with a curl-style `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n   - Send the file as a real multipart form field named `file`, equivalent to `-F 'file=@image.jpg;type=image/jpeg'`.\n   - Do not manually synthesize the multipart boundary when a native multipart uploader is available.\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\n","new_string":"2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with a Python `requests.post(..., params=..., headers=..., files=...)` multipart request to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload`\n   - Send query params: `storage_ref=nodes_template`, `local_file_path=upload`, and `user_id=<telegram-user-id>`.\n   - Send the file as a real multipart form field named `file`.\n   - Set `accept: application/json`.\n   - Do not set `Content-Type: multipart/form-data` manually; let `requests` generate the boundary when `files=` is used.\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\",\"old_string\":\"2. Require the Telegram user id.\\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\\n3. Upload the image with a curl-style `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\\n   - Send the file as a real multipart form field named `file`, equivalent to `-F 'file=@image.jpg;type=image/jpeg'`.\\n   - Do not manually synthesize the multipart boundary when a native multipart uploader is available.\\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"2. Require the Telegram user id.\\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\\n3. Upload the image with a Python `requests.post(..., params=..., headers=..., files=...)` multipart request to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload`\\n   - Send query params: `storage_ref=nodes_template`, `local_file_path=upload`, and `user_id=<telegram-user-id>`.\\n   - Send the file as a real multipart form field named `file`.\\n   - Set `accept: application/json`.\\n   - Do not set `Content-Type: multipart/form-data` manually; let `requests` generate the boundary when `files=` is used.\\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_JbXnsHwf6PJyHRxcS5SzLffl|fc_01ab9eaf5e5ca29e0169bd85724a4c8191a4a157f248f72e34","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md","old_string":"Keep these values fixed:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload`\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\n","new_string":"Keep these values fixed:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_template`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload`\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\",\"old_string\":\"Keep these values fixed:\\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n- `local_file_path`: `upload`\\n- execution endpoint: `http